TOPICS COVERED
Windows installation and boot process
BIOS/UEFI, Secure Boot, Windows Recovery Environment, and system recovery.
File systems and permissions 
NTFS, file ownership, access permissions, hidden files, encryption, and storage management.
User accounts and access control 
Local accounts, user groups, administrator privileges, and the principle of least privilege.
Processes, services, and startup programs 
How applications run, how Windows services work, and how programs can start automatically.
Windows Registry and Task Scheduler 
How Windows stores configuration settings and manages scheduled tasks.
System logs and troubleshooting 
Using Event Viewer to examine system events and investigate problems.
Device management 
Understanding drivers, hardware IDs, and common device issues
Networking and command-line tools 
Practicing commands such as ipconfig, ping, tracert, nslookup, netstat, tasklist, and systeminfo.
